Z||000006||Philphine||11-03-2001||11:44 PM||||thanks for y'alls concern. licked my wounds some and assessed the damage. still looks like just tail lights and rear facia need to be replaced. actually the lights still work and i can drive it, but i think i'll at least swap out the lights before i do. also feels like the front facia on the chopper has a bit of wave to it, but it's just an extra facia i have sitting on the car till i decide where i'm going with it.<P>side note: that 3m urethane bumper repair has been tested more than i would have liked and passed. car got tapped in traffic lightly and it flexed with the bumper without delaminating. and now with the bumper warping it kept with the bumper and warped and deformed with it. guess i'll be getting more for the new facia when i get one. <P>monkeyman, the box is safe in the house. i got it for the chopper and i'm not ready to put it in yet.<P>it had been raining off and on all afternoon and evening and there is no electrical power to the shed and no types of heater. it's just for storage. really hard to believe it could just catch fire. thats really the worst part of the situation. if it was set, who and why?||||reg||1
